# Wrangler CLI cache (account name/email). Accidental commit of this is what
# failed gitleaks and TrackedTreeHygieneTests on the 2026-08-20 Better Stack push.
.wrangler/

# Local git identity mapping. Contains personal addresses. Git still reads
# a working-tree .mailmap when ignored; do not copy it into a public snapshot.
.mailmap

# Local game-mode simulator dumps (see simulator/README.md)
simulator/results/

# Auto-generated by next dev - canonical rules in .claude/rules/frontend.md
ui/AGENTS.md

# =========================
# Executed legal documents (DH.5 / 8a.2)
# =========================
# The signed or filed DPAs themselves stay out of git. ROPA.md records the version and date of each,
# which is what Art. 28(3) actually asks for; the PDFs live wherever your other signed contracts do.
# Two reasons this is a rule and not a preference: the Fly.io DPA is countersigned, so it carries a
# real signature and the controller's address, which PRIVACY.md deliberately does not publish; and
# CLAIMS.md's attribution plan contemplates making this repo public, at which point anything ever
# committed is in the history for good, `git rm` included. The 2026-08-19 relicense does not change
# that: once public, history is public.
docs/legal/*.pdf
